  30:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** 
  31:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** /**
  32:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * @ingroup groupFilters
  33:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** */
  34:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** 
  35:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** /**
  36:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * @defgroup BiquadCascadeDF2T Biquad Cascade IIR Filters Using a Direct Form II Transposed Structur
  37:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** *
  38:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * This set of functions implements arbitrary order recursive (IIR) filters using a transposed direc
  39:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * The filters are implemented as a cascade of second order Biquad sections.
  40:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * These functions provide a slight memory savings as compared to the direct form I Biquad filter fu
  41:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * Only floating-point data is supported.
  42:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** *
  43:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * This function operate on blocks of input and output data and each call to the function
  44:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * processes <code>blockSize</code> samples through the filter.
  45:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * <code>pSrc</code> points to the array of input data and
  46:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * <code>pDst</code> points to the array of output data.
  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * Both arrays contain <code>blockSize</code> values.
  48:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** *
  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * \par Algorithm
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * Each Biquad stage implements a second order filter using the difference equation:
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * <pre>
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** *    y[n] = b0 * x[n] + d1
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** *    d1 = b1 * x[n] + a1 * y[n] + d2
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** *    d2 = b2 * x[n] + a2 * y[n]
  55:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * </pre>
  56:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * where d1 and d2 represent the two state values.
  57:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** *
  58:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * \par
  59:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * A Biquad filter using a transposed Direct Form II structure is shown below.
  60:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * \image html BiquadDF2Transposed.gif "Single transposed Direct Form II Biquad"
  61:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * Coefficients <code>b0, b1, and b2 </code> multiply the input signal <code>x[n]</code> and are ref
  62:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * Coefficients <code>a1</code> and <code>a2</code> multiply the output signal <code>y[n]</code> and
  63:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * Pay careful attention to the sign of the feedback coefficients.
  64:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * Some design tools flip the sign of the feedback coefficients:
  65:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * <pre>
  66:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** *    y[n] = b0 * x[n] + d1;
  67:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** *    d1 = b1 * x[n] - a1 * y[n] + d2;
  68:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** *    d2 = b2 * x[n] - a2 * y[n];
  69:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * </pre>
  70:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * In this case the feedback coefficients <code>a1</code> and <code>a2</code> must be negated when u
  71:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** *
  72:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * \par
  73:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * Higher order filters are realized as a cascade of second order sections.
  74:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * <code>numStages</code> refers to the number of second order stages used.
  75:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * For example, an 8th order filter would be realized with <code>numStages=4</code> second order sta
  76:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * A 9th order filter would be realized with <code>numStages=5</code> second order stages with the
  77:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * coefficients for one of the stages configured as a first order filter (<code>b2=0</code> and <cod
  78:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** *
  79:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * \par
  80:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * <code>pState</code> points to the state variable array.
  81:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * Each Biquad stage has 2 state variables <code>d1</code> and <code>d2</code>.
  82:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * The state variables are arranged in the <code>pState</code> array as:
  83:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * <pre>
  84:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** *     {d11, d12, d21, d22, ...}
  85:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * </pre>
  86:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * where <code>d1x</code> refers to the state variables for the first Biquad and
ARM GAS  C:\Users\Lamp\AppData\Local\Temp\ccWUVyE8.s 			page 3


  87:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * <code>d2x</code> refers to the state variables for the second Biquad.
  88:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * The state array has a total length of <code>2*numStages</code> values.
  89:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * The state variables are updated after each block of data is processed; the coefficients are untou
  90:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** *
  91:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * \par
  92:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * The CMSIS library contains Biquad filters in both Direct Form I and transposed Direct Form II.
  93:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * The advantage of the Direct Form I structure is that it is numerically more robust for fixed-poin
  94:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * That is why the Direct Form I structure supports Q15 and Q31 data types.
  95:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * The transposed Direct Form II structure, on the other hand, requires a wide dynamic range for the
  96:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * Because of this, the CMSIS library only has a floating-point version of the Direct Form II Biquad
  97:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * The advantage of the Direct Form II Biquad is that it requires half the number of state variables
  98:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** *
  99:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * \par Instance Structure
 100:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * The coefficients and state variables for a filter are stored together in an instance data structu
 101:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * A separate instance structure must be defined for each filter.
 102:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * Coefficient arrays may be shared among several instances while state variable arrays cannot be sh
 103:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** *
 104:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * \par Init Functions
 105:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * There is also an associated initialization function.
 106:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * The initialization function performs following operations:
 107:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * - Sets the values of the internal structure fields.
 108:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * - Zeros out the values in the state buffer.
 109:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * To do this manually without calling the init function, assign the follow subfields of the instanc
 110:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * numStages, pCoeffs, pState. Also set all of the values in pState to zero.
 111:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** *
 112:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * \par
 113:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * Use of the initialization function is optional.
 114:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * However, if the initialization function is used, then the instance structure cannot be placed int
 115:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * To place an instance structure into a const data section, the instance structure must be manually
 116:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * Set the values in the state buffer to zeros before static initialization.
 117:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * For example, to statically initialize the instance structure use
 118:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * <pre>
 119:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** *     arm_biquad_cascade_df2T_instance_f32 S1 = {numStages, pState, pCoeffs};
 120:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * </pre>
 121:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * where <code>numStages</code> is the number of Biquad stages in the filter; <code>pState</code> is
 122:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * <code>pCoeffs</code> is the address of the coefficient buffer;
 123:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** *
 124:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** */
 125:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** 
 126:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** /**
 127:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * @addtogroup BiquadCascadeDF2T
 128:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * @{
 129:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** */
 130:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** 
 131:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** /**
 132:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * @brief Processing function for the floating-point transposed direct form II Biquad cascade filter
 133:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * @param[in]  *S        points to an instance of the filter data structure.
 134:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * @param[in]  *pSrc     points to the block of input data.
 135:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * @param[out] *pDst     points to the block of output data
 136:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * @param[in]  blockSize number of samples to process.
 137:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** * @return none.
 138:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** */
 139:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_biquad_cascade_stereo_df2T_f32.c **** 
